{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos-249-binary-totient-series","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#cor:integral-normal-form","Integral coordinates and all integral\nrelations","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. The retained family is a\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>-basis of the module generated by\nthe sections through level <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi></math></span>. Index\nthe sections by their level and residue, retaining distinct indices even\nwhen they define equal sequences. For each omitted index <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>i</mi></math></span>, write the scalar reduction as <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub></math></span>, where <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is retained and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span> is a nonnegative integer. In the free\nabelian group with one generator <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span> for each of these indices, the\nvectors </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mtext> omitted</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> form a <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>-basis\nof the kernel of evaluation <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span>. In particular, every integral relation has a unique\nintegral expression in these elementary relations, and their rank is\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#cor:periodic-freezing","Periodic coefficients","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math></span> be pairwise\nnonproportional affine forms with integer coefficients and positive\nslopes. If <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math></span> are\nrational-valued periodic sequences, then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>for all sufficiently large </mtext><mi>n</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>for every </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#lem:bounded-pulse","An isolated nonzero coefficient between\nlong zero blocks","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></math></span>. Suppose that for arbitrarily\nlarge <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>L</mi></math></span> there is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>L</mi></math></span> such that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> is\nirrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#res:basis","Dyadic basis","<p><em> The family </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>∪</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>r</mi><mtext> odd</mtext><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> is a basis for the rational\nspan of the full dyadic kernel. Every rational relation is generated by\nthe scalar reductions. The complete level-zero truncation has dimension\none.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#res:fulldepth","Propagation of one nonintegral tail\ndifference","<p><em> Fix <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span>, then every\nsufficiently late pair <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>\ncontains an <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi></math></span> such that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> holds. Consequently </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Requiring\nthis for every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> is\nequivalent to <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#res:rankonefloor","A lower bound for the rank-one\nquotients","<p><em> For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Y</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>, the denominator of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is positive, and the unique\nminimiser is <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. Every\nadmissible quotient and every nonempty finite positive weighted average\nof such quotients satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>320</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The\nuniform bound <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>15</mn></math></span> is\nfalse already at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#res:residueseries","Series of totient residues","<p><em> For\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>\nand <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>, the series\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo lspace=\"0.278em\" rspace=\"0.278em\">mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math></span>\nis rational exactly when <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi></math></span> is\nconstant on the even residue classes. If that constant is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>, its value is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>3</mn><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-249-binary-totient-series#thm:kkernelrank","A basis through each finite level","<p><em>\nLet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> be integers, write <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and put\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>span</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>dim</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mrow><mi>ℬ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>∪</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> is a basis. Every omitted section reduces to a basis\nelement by an explicit scalar: <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></span> for\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>u</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>∣</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>u</mi></math></span>, then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mi>u</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">(</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.623em\" maxsize=\"1.623em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"]]}
